       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (850 mg three times daily). The risks at that dose include lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nHere are some things the order might have been meant to say:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max dose.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg twice daily**, a more typical regimen. It's often started at 500 mg once or twice daily and titrated up.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your resident or attending. Once you have the correct dose, tell me and I'll enter it. I can also add a note such as \"give with meals.\""
      }
